From 00ff104149eaaddf84dfb4756389852ae35e99cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Walther <tederific@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:17:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Base64: public, with an optional Padded parameter

CryptoLib.Base64 was a private child, reachable only from inside the crate.
Make it public and give Encoded_Length, Decoded_Length, Encode and Decode a
Padded parameter (default False, so existing callers are unchanged): RFC 4648
section 4 padding with '='.  Decoding stays strict: whole groups only, at most
two '=' at the end, the unused low bits zero.

Decode now zeroes its output on every refusal.  It used to leave the octets of
the groups read before the bad one, against the crate's rule that a failed
operation leaves nothing partial.

Tests: Check_Base64 (RFC 4648 section 10 vectors in both forms, a round trip at
every length from 0 to 64, and the refusals, each asserting the zeroed
output).  README package map and SECURITY.md updated.
